1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,428
So our gathering today has a name,

2
00:00:02,428 --> 00:00:05,356
and it's called "Your Sins Are Forgiven."

3
00:00:05,356 --> 00:00:07,784
You might find that a bit abrupt —

4
00:00:07,784 --> 00:00:09,783
our very first time meeting,

5
00:00:09,783 --> 00:00:12,854
so why talk about your sins being
forgiven?

6
00:00:12,854 --> 00:00:15,282
Now, there's a picture next to me,

7
00:00:15,282 --> 00:00:16,638
an image beside me,

8
00:00:16,638 --> 00:00:18,352
and that image, in fact,

9
00:00:18,352 --> 00:00:20,637
comes from this book right here.

10
00:00:20,637 --> 00:00:23,851
I don't know if you can see, here in my
hand,

11
00:00:23,851 --> 00:00:26,136
I'm holding this book right now.

12
00:00:26,136 --> 00:00:27,207
And this book —

13
00:00:27,207 --> 00:00:30,063
well, I doubt many people could read it,

14
00:00:30,063 --> 00:00:32,277
because it's written in Nepali.

15
00:00:32,277 --> 00:00:34,419
I bought it over in Kathmandu,

16
00:00:34,419 --> 00:00:34,919
and so,

17
00:00:34,919 --> 00:00:38,990
this here is an event from the Lord Jesus'
life on earth.

18
00:00:38,990 --> 00:00:42,703
We'll have a chance to talk about it a
little later.

19
00:00:42,703 --> 00:00:44,988
Just now, after you heard Killy,

20
00:00:44,988 --> 00:00:47,416
and after you heard Sai-fai share,

21
00:00:47,416 --> 00:00:50,772
I wonder if you envy the change in their
lives.

22
00:00:50,772 --> 00:00:54,271
It makes me think of this one verse in the
Bible.

23
00:00:54,271 --> 00:00:55,485
What does it say?

24
00:00:55,485 --> 00:00:58,413
It is the One who girds us with strength,

25
00:00:58,413 --> 00:01:00,270
and makes our way perfect;

26
00:01:00,270 --> 00:01:00,984
He is God.

27
00:01:00,984 --> 00:01:06,411
The God we come to know today isn't just a
doctrine — He is a living Person.

28
00:01:06,411 --> 00:01:10,196
Some people say you become like the
company you keep.

29
00:01:10,196 --> 00:01:15,837
You'll find that those who believe in God
have changed lives, real experiences,

30
00:01:15,837 --> 00:01:21,621
and they change for the better. From this
you see God is not only real, but good.

31
00:01:21,621 --> 00:01:26,406
He is the One who girds us with strength
and makes our way perfect.

32
00:01:26,406 --> 00:01:30,333
And I hope that today, through coming to
know this God,

33
00:01:30,333 --> 00:01:33,332
your life, too, will be changed like this.

34
00:01:33,332 --> 00:01:35,475
On my desk there's an ornament

35
00:01:35,475 --> 00:01:38,545
that constantly reminds me how real God
is.

36
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:41,421
Can you see what I'm holding in my hand?

37
00:01:41,421 --> 00:01:43,281
It might be a little dark.

38
00:01:43,281 --> 00:01:46,572
It's actually a magnetically levitating
globe.

39
00:01:46,572 --> 00:01:50,077
Sometimes I buy little things as gifts to
myself,

40
00:01:50,077 --> 00:01:53,154
and this globe — what does it remind me
of?

41
00:01:53,154 --> 00:01:57,088
Well, long ago many people believed the
earth was flat.

42
00:01:57,088 --> 00:02:02,024
In fact, to this day there's even an
International Flat Earth Society

43
00:02:02,024 --> 00:02:04,170
that claims the earth is flat.

44
00:02:04,170 --> 00:02:06,459
So the people of old used to say

45
00:02:06,459 --> 00:02:10,966
that sailing the seas and racing horses
each carry their risks.

46
00:02:10,966 --> 00:02:11,825
Why is that?

47
00:02:11,825 --> 00:02:13,899
Why was sailing so dangerous?

48
00:02:13,899 --> 00:02:16,761
Because they thought the earth was flat.

49
00:02:16,761 --> 00:02:18,478
If you went too far out,

50
00:02:18,478 --> 00:02:20,481
you would fall off the edge,

51
00:02:20,481 --> 00:02:22,985
tumbling down like off a waterfall.

52
00:02:22,985 --> 00:02:24,630
So the seafarers of old

53
00:02:24,630 --> 00:02:27,277
would hug the coastline as they went,

54
00:02:27,277 --> 00:02:29,852
sailing a while, then back to shore,

55
00:02:29,852 --> 00:02:32,213
a while more, then back to shore,

56
00:02:32,213 --> 00:02:34,860
never daring to cross the open ocean,

57
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:38,222
because they feared falling off that
waterfall.

58
00:02:38,222 --> 00:02:39,581
And you'll notice —

59
00:02:39,581 --> 00:02:41,799
when did people finally realize

60
00:02:41,799 --> 00:02:44,159
that the earth is actually round?

61
00:02:44,159 --> 00:02:45,948
Well, going back to this,

62
00:02:45,948 --> 00:02:48,523
you see there are two pictures here.

63
00:02:48,523 --> 00:02:50,526
Going back to the Greek era,

64
00:02:50,526 --> 00:02:52,601
back to around 200 or 300 BC,

65
00:02:52,601 --> 00:02:55,605
some people began to wonder and to reason.

66
00:02:55,605 --> 00:02:56,464
What was it?

67
00:02:56,464 --> 00:02:58,896
when they watched a lunar eclipse,

68
00:02:58,896 --> 00:03:01,114
there was a shadow on the moon.

69
00:03:01,114 --> 00:03:01,758
That is —

70
00:03:01,758 --> 00:03:03,975
the earth was blocking the sun,

71
00:03:03,975 --> 00:03:06,908
and the shadow it cast had a curve to it.

72
00:03:06,908 --> 00:03:09,555
so they guessed the earth was curved.

73
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:13,440
For instance, there were others who
noticed something as well,

74
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:14,503
and it was this —

75
00:03:14,503 --> 00:03:16,631
that on one and the very same day,

76
00:03:16,631 --> 00:03:18,383
yet in two different places,

77
00:03:18,383 --> 00:03:21,699
the shadows cast by the sun were not the
same at all.

78
00:03:21,699 --> 00:03:25,516
Over in Egypt, the shadow would fall
perfectly straight down,

79
00:03:25,516 --> 00:03:27,831
but a few hundred miles further away,

80
00:03:27,831 --> 00:03:31,022
that very same shadow fell at a slant, at
an angle.

81
00:03:31,022 --> 00:03:34,652
And from that, they guessed that the earth
must be curved.

82
00:03:34,652 --> 00:03:38,969
But when was it that people finally proved
the earth really is round?

83
00:03:38,969 --> 00:03:42,911
It wasn't until the Middle Ages, right
around the 16th century.

84
00:03:42,911 --> 00:03:46,478
So why is it that Columbus and Magellan
became so famous?

85
00:03:46,478 --> 00:03:51,546
It's because their discoveries were made
at the genuine risk of their very lives.

86
00:03:51,546 --> 00:03:59,305
Because out on an ocean voyage, if the
earth really had been flat, they would set
sail and never be able to turn back again.

87
00:03:59,305 --> 00:04:05,250
But as it turns out, the Bible has a verse
that says exactly this, over in the book
of Isaiah —

88
00:04:05,250 --> 00:04:09,442
And when was the book of Isaiah written?
It was around the 700s BC,

89
00:04:09,442 --> 00:04:12,508
roughly the time of China's Eastern Zhou
dynasty,

90
00:04:12,508 --> 00:04:15,449
even earlier than the Spring and Autumn
period.

91
00:04:15,449 --> 00:04:19,829
The Bible says this: God sits enthroned
above the circle of the earth.

92
00:04:19,829 --> 00:04:24,897
So the Bible told us this long, long ago —
2,700 years ago it had already told us

93
00:04:24,897 --> 00:04:26,962
that the earth is a great circle.

94
00:04:26,962 --> 00:04:32,782
And the original word even carries the
sense of something solid, something
three-dimensional.

95
00:04:32,782 --> 00:04:37,287
That's why some English versions render it
as "the sphere of the earth,"

96
00:04:37,287 --> 00:04:40,353
meaning upon the round globe of the earth
itself.

97
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:42,044
Here's another example.

98
00:04:42,044 --> 00:04:46,657
People long ago thought the earth must be
hung up by something,

99
00:04:46,657 --> 00:04:48,194
held up by something,

100
00:04:48,194 --> 00:04:50,757
because if nothing were hanging it,

101
00:04:50,757 --> 00:04:52,368
nothing holding it up,

102
00:04:52,368 --> 00:04:54,344
it would just keep falling.

103
00:04:54,344 --> 00:04:57,786
But do any of you feel like you're
falling? No.

104
00:04:57,786 --> 00:05:00,641
So surely something must be hanging it,

105
00:05:00,641 --> 00:05:02,398
something holding it up.

106
00:05:02,398 --> 00:05:05,913
So you'll find that in myths all over the
world,

107
00:05:05,913 --> 00:05:08,329
there are legends just like this.

108
00:05:08,329 --> 00:05:11,477
Some picture the earth carried on a
turtle,

109
00:05:11,477 --> 00:05:13,308
some on a great elephant,

110
00:05:13,308 --> 00:05:16,017
some on the shoulders of a strongman.

111
00:05:16,017 --> 00:05:19,385
Maybe, who knows, after holding it up so
long,

112
00:05:19,385 --> 00:05:20,776
he shifts a little,

113
00:05:20,776 --> 00:05:23,046
and then you get an earthquake.

114
00:05:23,046 --> 00:05:25,242
That's how it is in the myths,

115
00:05:25,242 --> 00:05:27,072
in the human imagination.

116
00:05:27,072 --> 00:05:29,635
But the Bible tells us it isn't so.

117
00:05:29,635 --> 00:05:34,321
The book of Job is even older than the
Isaiah we just mentioned,

118
00:05:34,321 --> 00:05:36,737
perhaps 3,500 to 4,000 years ago,

119
00:05:36,737 --> 00:05:38,568
around 1,500 to 2,000 BC.

120
00:05:38,568 --> 00:05:40,691
And the Bible has this verse:

121
00:05:40,691 --> 00:05:43,912
He stretches out the north over empty
space,

122
00:05:43,912 --> 00:05:46,182
and hangs the earth on nothing.

123
00:05:46,182 --> 00:05:48,891
The Chinese doesn't quite capture it,

124
00:05:48,891 --> 00:05:51,161
so how does the English put it?

125
00:05:51,161 --> 00:05:52,406
What does it say?

126
00:05:52,406 --> 00:05:55,407
It says God "hangs the earth on nothing."

127
00:05:55,407 --> 00:05:59,727
That is, God hung the earth without
anything holding it up.

128
00:05:59,727 --> 00:06:01,338
Isn't that remarkable?

129
00:06:01,338 --> 00:06:07,928
So let me ask you: when did we learn the
earth truly hangs on nothing, held up by
nothing?

130
00:06:07,928 --> 00:06:10,783
When did the solid proof actually come?

131
00:06:10,783 --> 00:06:13,272
Not until rockets rose into space.

132
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:17,926
And when the astronauts finally looked
back at the earth, what did they find?

133
00:06:17,926 --> 00:06:21,003
Why, there really was no great elephant
down there,

134
00:06:21,003 --> 00:06:24,382
and truly no strongman's shoulders holding
it up at all.

135
00:06:24,382 --> 00:06:28,907
And on top of all that, there were the
great expeditions to the North Pole,

136
00:06:28,907 --> 00:06:31,984
and the expeditions down to the South Pole
as well.

137
00:06:31,984 --> 00:06:35,604
Even the very farthest places on earth
were finally reached,

138
00:06:35,604 --> 00:06:37,897
and still they found no rope anywhere,

139
00:06:37,897 --> 00:06:39,224
nothing hanging it up,

140
00:06:39,224 --> 00:06:41,457
and nothing holding it up from below.

141
00:06:41,457 --> 00:06:44,836
Yet already, more than three or four
thousand years ago,

142
00:06:44,836 --> 00:06:47,128
the Bible had told us this very thing:

143
00:06:47,128 --> 00:06:47,732
that God —

144
00:06:47,732 --> 00:06:49,663
"He hangs the earth on nothing."

145
00:06:49,663 --> 00:06:51,473
And here is yet another verse.

146
00:06:51,473 --> 00:06:54,791
It says: Have you, in your days, commanded
the morning,

147
00:06:54,791 --> 00:06:55,937
and caused the dawn

148
00:06:55,937 --> 00:06:57,024
to know its place,

149
00:06:57,024 --> 00:07:01,126
so that by this light the earth is changed
like clay under the seal?

150
00:07:01,126 --> 00:07:03,117
Now what on earth does that mean?

151
00:07:03,117 --> 00:07:07,401
Well, it's describing that very moment of
sunrise early in the morning,

152
00:07:07,401 --> 00:07:10,358
as the ground slowly grows brighter and
brighter,

153
00:07:10,358 --> 00:07:14,461
and the light spreads across it like a
seal being pressed into clay.

154
00:07:14,461 --> 00:07:16,210
What am I even talking about?

155
00:07:16,210 --> 00:07:20,434
Do you know how people in the old days
used to make a seal impression?

156
00:07:20,434 --> 00:07:24,778
They would carve their patterns and
letters onto a round stone cylinder,

157
00:07:24,778 --> 00:07:28,097
then they would prepare a flat, smooth
surface of clay,

158
00:07:28,097 --> 00:07:30,812
and roll that cylinder right across the
clay.

159
00:07:30,812 --> 00:07:35,397
And after the pressing, don't all the
patterns and letters come out onto it?

160
00:07:35,397 --> 00:07:39,440
And that same stone seal could then be
used to print a second time,

161
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:41,431
and even a third time after that.

162
00:07:41,431 --> 00:07:45,473
That's exactly how the people back then
made all their impressions.

163
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:51,081
So why would the sunrise be likened to a
seal on clay? What is it really picturing
for us?

164
00:07:51,081 --> 00:07:56,121
You notice how it grows brighter and
brighter, the darkness slowly receding
away,

165
00:07:56,121 --> 00:08:00,291
and the changing of the whole earth is
just like that rolling seal,

166
00:08:00,291 --> 00:08:06,389
as if to show us that the earth, like a
rolling seal, actually turns — it rotates
on its own axis.

167
00:08:06,389 --> 00:08:08,567
And not only does the earth rotate,

168
00:08:08,567 --> 00:08:10,123
it also happens to tilt —

169
00:08:10,123 --> 00:08:11,865
tilted over at 23.5 degrees.

170
00:08:11,865 --> 00:08:19,831
And what effect does that have? Well, it's
because of that very 23.5-degree tilt that
we get spring, summer, autumn, and winter.

171
00:08:19,831 --> 00:08:22,133
So in just a couple of days from now,

172
00:08:22,133 --> 00:08:25,929
it will be the winter solstice up in the
Northern Hemisphere,

173
00:08:25,929 --> 00:08:31,405
while down in the Southern Hemisphere it
may well be the longest day of the entire
year.

174
00:08:31,405 --> 00:08:35,077
Now don't the four seasons make life so
much more colorful?

175
00:08:35,077 --> 00:08:37,815
And they serve a very practical purpose
too,

176
00:08:37,815 --> 00:08:41,238
because when the earth is tilted on its
axis like this,

177
00:08:41,238 --> 00:08:44,100
you find that many more regions become
warmer,

178
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:46,092
and far more livable for people,

179
00:08:46,092 --> 00:08:49,701
so the habitable areas of the world
increase a great deal.

180
00:08:49,701 --> 00:08:56,297
If it spun straight up with no tilt at
all, the middle would be scorching hot and
the poles freezing cold.

181
00:08:56,297 --> 00:08:59,098
So why is the Bible so utterly
extraordinary?

182
00:08:59,098 --> 00:09:02,520
It says so very much about the earth and
about science,

183
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:05,321
so why on earth is it so remarkably
accurate?

184
00:09:05,321 --> 00:09:09,117
Even running ahead of what so many would
only later discover,

185
00:09:09,117 --> 00:09:13,659
things that could only be proven with hard
evidence many years afterward.

186
00:09:13,659 --> 00:09:16,584
It's because the Bible is the very word of
God.

187
00:09:16,584 --> 00:09:18,582
Just as the Bible says here,

188
00:09:18,582 --> 00:09:21,221
All Scripture is breathed out by God.

189
00:09:21,221 --> 00:09:23,290
The Bible is the word of God.

190
00:09:23,290 --> 00:09:28,997
This heaven and earth was made by God, so
of course He knows every detail of it,

191
00:09:28,997 --> 00:09:33,491
and so through the Bible God lets us come
to know these things.

192
00:09:33,491 --> 00:09:38,984
So through all we've said, you can know
the One in the Bible is the true God,

193
00:09:38,984 --> 00:09:43,835
and through the Bible we also come to know
how real the true God is.

194
00:09:43,835 --> 00:09:46,404
And it's not only through the Bible.

195
00:09:46,404 --> 00:09:52,824
You'll notice — when you have time, why do
people love to travel, to head out into
nature?

196
00:09:52,824 --> 00:09:54,465
Because it's beautiful.

197
00:09:54,465 --> 00:09:58,174
When you take in the created world, you
find it is —

198
00:09:58,174 --> 00:09:58,817
so grand,

199
00:09:58,817 --> 00:09:59,744
so wonderful,

200
00:09:59,744 --> 00:10:00,671
so intricate,

201
00:10:00,671 --> 00:10:01,599
so beautiful.

202
00:10:01,599 --> 00:10:07,877
The Bible has a verse — what does it say?
It says: ever since the creation of the
world,

203
00:10:07,877 --> 00:10:09,232
God's eternal power

204
00:10:09,232 --> 00:10:10,730
His everlasting power

205
00:10:10,730 --> 00:10:14,297
and His divine nature — that is, what He
is like —

206
00:10:14,297 --> 00:10:15,510
are clearly seen.

207
00:10:15,510 --> 00:10:17,293
Though unseen by the eye,

208
00:10:17,293 --> 00:10:19,719
yet through the things He has made

209
00:10:19,719 --> 00:10:21,359
they can be understood,

210
00:10:21,359 --> 00:10:23,500
leaving people without excuse.

211
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:28,636
So through the created world — the more
you go outdoors and look around,

212
00:10:28,636 --> 00:10:30,990
you'll come to know God too. Why?

213
00:10:30,990 --> 00:10:34,557
Because you see the world, and isn't it
wonderful?

214
00:10:34,557 --> 00:10:38,124
It's like this watch you see in my hand
right now.

215
00:10:38,124 --> 00:10:41,976
When you look at the watch, isn't it
beautifully made?

216
00:10:41,976 --> 00:10:45,187
Surely someone designed it, someone built
it.

217
00:10:45,187 --> 00:10:48,325
And the beauty of this world, its
intricacy,

218
00:10:48,325 --> 00:10:50,894
is far more complex than this watch.

219
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,045
So when I look at this world,

220
00:10:53,045 --> 00:10:56,298
I know there truly is a Designer, a
Creator.

221
00:10:56,298 --> 00:10:58,961
And God truly did create all things.

222
00:10:58,961 --> 00:11:00,957
Now there was once a survey

223
00:11:00,957 --> 00:11:05,764
of some of the most eminent scientists of
the last few centuries.

224
00:11:05,764 --> 00:11:07,687
What did that survey find?

225
00:11:07,687 --> 00:11:12,642
Among the scientists surveyed, over ninety
percent believed in God.

226
00:11:12,642 --> 00:11:17,301
So let me tell you — believing in God is
not rejecting science.

227
00:11:17,301 --> 00:11:22,403
More than ninety percent of those
scientists believed there is a God.

228
00:11:22,403 --> 00:11:27,950
Why? Because the more they researched, the
more they understood this world,

229
00:11:27,950 --> 00:11:32,313
the more they realized there must be a
Designer, a Creator.

230
00:11:32,313 --> 00:11:36,232
So believing in God today is in fact very
reasonable.

231
00:11:36,232 --> 00:11:39,782
This study was even published in the
newspapers.

232
00:11:39,782 --> 00:11:43,036
I wonder if you happened to notice the
news.

233
00:11:43,036 --> 00:11:44,884
As we come to this point,

234
00:11:44,884 --> 00:11:48,582
you'll find that the God we are speaking
of today,

235
00:11:48,582 --> 00:11:50,801
the God recorded in the Bible,

236
00:11:50,801 --> 00:11:54,350
is the Creator of heaven, earth, and all
things.

237
00:11:54,350 --> 00:11:56,569
He is not made by human hands.

238
00:11:56,569 --> 00:12:01,080
As someone once put it, the true God is
the One who made man,

239
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:03,964
who made heaven, earth, and all things.

240
00:12:03,964 --> 00:12:05,961
A false god is made by man.

241
00:12:05,961 --> 00:12:08,845
And the Bible says false gods have eyes

242
00:12:08,845 --> 00:12:09,954
but cannot see,

243
00:12:09,954 --> 00:12:11,877
have ears but cannot hear,

244
00:12:11,877 --> 00:12:14,021
have mouths but cannot speak.

245
00:12:14,021 --> 00:12:17,201
They can't be bought or sold in the
market,

246
00:12:17,201 --> 00:12:19,124
and they never go on sale.

247
00:12:21,220 --> 00:12:24,951
And besides, you just heard Killy's
testimony a moment ago,

248
00:12:24,951 --> 00:12:27,608
and you heard Sai-fai's testimony as well,

249
00:12:27,608 --> 00:12:32,224
and you could see from them that God
really is kind, and that He is good.

250
00:12:32,224 --> 00:12:37,916
Now some people — say, those in the
triads, the gangs — will worship idols and
false gods.

251
00:12:37,916 --> 00:12:44,304
The gangsters will pray that all their
whoring, their gambling, and their
drinking go along smoothly.

252
00:12:44,304 --> 00:12:49,300
And funnily enough, the police station
right there worships the very same idol.

253
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:52,209
So the next time your robbery happens to
fail,

254
00:12:52,209 --> 00:12:59,545
you might just want to wonder whether the
very god you worship tipped them off —
whether he turned informant on you.

255
00:12:59,545 --> 00:13:06,628
So from all of this you can clearly see:
this God is the Creator of heaven and all
things, and He is truly good.

256
00:13:06,628 --> 00:13:09,537
The Bible lets us know this: that God is
love.

257
00:13:09,537 --> 00:13:15,356
God so greatly desires that people would
receive all of His goodness, and all of
His riches.

258
00:13:15,356 --> 00:13:19,783
And so He sent His only begotten Son — God
sent His one and only Son —

259
00:13:19,783 --> 00:13:23,451
in order to let people come to know Him,
and to help them.

260
00:13:23,451 --> 00:13:26,803
Now concerning the Lord Jesus coming into
the world —

261
00:13:26,803 --> 00:13:30,344
there are a great many prophecies about it
in the Bible.

262
00:13:30,344 --> 00:13:33,380
And as the word itself suggests, a
prophecy is —

263
00:13:33,380 --> 00:13:36,099
something that has not yet happened at
all,

264
00:13:36,099 --> 00:13:38,945
and yet is foretold and announced in
advance.

265
00:13:38,945 --> 00:13:41,602
In fact, concerning the Lord Jesus' birth,

266
00:13:41,602 --> 00:13:44,890
the Bible foretold the very time when He
would come,

267
00:13:44,890 --> 00:13:47,546
and the very place where He would be born,

268
00:13:47,546 --> 00:13:49,760
and even what He was coming to do —

269
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:52,416
over three hundred such prophecies in all.

270
00:13:52,420 --> 00:13:54,804
Their purpose is to let us know,

271
00:13:54,804 --> 00:13:57,262
so that when the Lord Jesus came,

272
00:13:57,262 --> 00:13:59,125
we would not mistake Him.

273
00:13:59,125 --> 00:14:01,062
He is the Savior God sent.

274
00:14:01,062 --> 00:14:02,626
He is the Son of God.

275
00:14:02,626 --> 00:14:04,116
Here is one example.

276
00:14:04,116 --> 00:14:07,021
We know that at Christmas, coming soon,

277
00:14:07,021 --> 00:14:09,256
where was the Lord Jesus born?

278
00:14:09,256 --> 00:14:10,970
In Bethlehem of Israel.

279
00:14:10,970 --> 00:14:13,875
Now in the Old Testament book of Micah,

280
00:14:13,875 --> 00:14:15,365
around the 700s BC —

281
00:14:15,365 --> 00:14:20,282
that is, some seven hundred years before
the Lord Jesus was born —

282
00:14:20,282 --> 00:14:23,038
there was already a saying like this.

283
00:14:23,038 --> 00:14:24,304
What does it say?

284
00:14:24,304 --> 00:14:27,135
It says: But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah,

285
00:14:27,135 --> 00:14:30,637
though you are little among the towns of
Judah,

286
00:14:30,637 --> 00:14:32,499
out of you shall come One

287
00:14:32,499 --> 00:14:34,510
who will come forth for Me,

288
00:14:34,510 --> 00:14:35,628
to be the ruler

289
00:14:35,628 --> 00:14:36,373
in Israel,

290
00:14:36,373 --> 00:14:37,341
whose origins

291
00:14:37,341 --> 00:14:38,533
are from of old,

292
00:14:38,533 --> 00:14:39,949
from ancient times.

293
00:14:39,949 --> 00:14:42,631
These two lines say it very clearly.

294
00:14:42,631 --> 00:14:44,344
"Bethlehem Ephrathah" —

295
00:14:44,344 --> 00:14:48,814
"little among the towns of Judah" — so
it's a town, a place.

296
00:14:48,814 --> 00:14:52,017
Bethlehem was originally a very small
town,

297
00:14:52,017 --> 00:14:54,699
but a King would come forth from it,

298
00:14:54,699 --> 00:14:56,636
to be the ruler in Israel.

299
00:14:56,636 --> 00:15:00,361
A king coming forth — that alone isn't so
strange.

300
00:15:00,361 --> 00:15:03,639
Even a king emerging, small as the town is
—

301
00:15:03,639 --> 00:15:06,916
a small town producing a king isn't
strange.

302
00:15:06,916 --> 00:15:08,630
That could well happen.

303
00:15:08,630 --> 00:15:10,865
But notice the very last line.

304
00:15:10,865 --> 00:15:12,280
It says His origins

305
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:15,037
have existed from the very beginning.

306
00:15:15,037 --> 00:15:18,463
Apart from God, who could meet this
condition?

307
00:15:18,463 --> 00:15:21,071
Only the self-existent, eternal God

308
00:15:21,071 --> 00:15:22,114
could meet it.

309
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:31,785
So from this one verse we know that
Bethlehem would see not merely some king
appear,

310
00:15:31,785 --> 00:15:34,368
but rather, what kind of King would it be?

311
00:15:34,368 --> 00:15:40,455
It would be the Son of God Himself
entering the world, the One whose origins
are from all eternity.

312
00:15:40,455 --> 00:15:43,099
Now when the Lord Jesus came to this
earth,

313
00:15:43,099 --> 00:15:45,436
He went all about the land doing good,

314
00:15:45,436 --> 00:15:47,834
and He performed a great many miracles,

315
00:15:47,834 --> 00:15:49,925
and He helped so very many people.

316
00:15:49,925 --> 00:15:51,831
He opened the eyes of the blind

317
00:15:51,831 --> 00:15:54,106
and made them able to see once again.

318
00:15:54,106 --> 00:15:57,180
And I wonder, at this very stage of your
own life,

319
00:15:57,180 --> 00:16:00,993
just how much you have really come to
understand about living.

320
00:16:00,993 --> 00:16:04,498
Are you perhaps still groping your way
about in the dark,

321
00:16:04,498 --> 00:16:06,342
still feeling lost and adrift,

322
00:16:06,342 --> 00:16:09,232
not knowing what the meaning of life
really is,

323
00:16:09,232 --> 00:16:12,245
not even knowing what it is you're chasing
after?

324
00:16:12,245 --> 00:16:15,197
The Lord Jesus came and gave sight to the
blind,

325
00:16:15,197 --> 00:16:18,640
and in the same way He brings real light
into our lives.

326
00:16:18,640 --> 00:16:23,928
He also once stood up and stilled the very
wind and the waves in the midst of a
storm.

327
00:16:23,928 --> 00:16:26,572
He is able to rescue our lives from
danger,

328
00:16:26,572 --> 00:16:29,524
and He is just as able to calm the raging
storm.

329
00:16:29,524 --> 00:16:32,906
In your life you will sometimes meet with
circumstances

330
00:16:32,906 --> 00:16:35,857
that press in hard upon you like a fierce
storm,

331
00:16:35,857 --> 00:16:37,948
leaving you anxious and unsettled,

332
00:16:37,948 --> 00:16:41,145
and making you feel as though you're in
real danger.

333
00:16:41,145 --> 00:16:43,482
But the Lord is well able to help you,

334
00:16:43,482 --> 00:16:46,126
calming every last storm within your
heart,

335
00:16:46,126 --> 00:16:48,524
and carrying you safely through it all.

336
00:16:48,524 --> 00:16:50,000
He was also able to make

337
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,783
the lame man get up and walk.

338
00:16:51,783 --> 00:16:57,317
And He cast out many unclean spirits,
setting free all those who were possessed
by demons.

339
00:16:57,317 --> 00:17:02,605
Perhaps some of you feel that your lives
are bound up tightly by so very many
things —

340
00:17:02,605 --> 00:17:05,249
some bad old habits, perhaps a foul
temper,

341
00:17:05,249 --> 00:17:07,955
an unhealthy way of living, or certain
sins,

342
00:17:07,955 --> 00:17:15,764
some perhaps even troubled by evil spirits
— and you'll find that the Lord is able to
help with all of it, and to set you free.

343
00:17:15,764 --> 00:17:20,529
He even once raised the dead back to life,
giving life itself back to people.

344
00:17:20,529 --> 00:17:23,995
So besides fulfilling so many of the
Bible's prophecies,

345
00:17:23,995 --> 00:17:28,327
and showing us plainly that He is the
Savior God had promised to send,

346
00:17:28,327 --> 00:17:31,855
through the very things that the Lord
Jesus actually did,

347
00:17:31,855 --> 00:17:35,630
we also come to know that He is the very
One God was sending.

348
00:17:35,630 --> 00:17:39,344
Now at the very beginning I mentioned this
little book here.

349
00:17:39,344 --> 00:17:42,871
So what story is it that this little book
actually tells?

350
00:17:42,871 --> 00:17:47,451
Well, it tells of a paralyzed man, and his
own experience of being healed,

351
00:17:47,451 --> 00:17:50,360
and it's recorded for us in the Gospel of
Mark.

352
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:52,898
So what exactly happened in this account?

353
00:17:52,898 --> 00:17:56,920
At the time, the Lord Jesus had come to a
place called Capernaum.

354
00:17:56,920 --> 00:18:01,191
And from this detail too you can see that
the Bible is real and true.

355
00:18:01,191 --> 00:18:05,028
It doesn't just say "long, long ago, in a
land far, far away,"

356
00:18:05,028 --> 00:18:08,184
all vague and dreamlike like that — no,
not at all.

357
00:18:08,184 --> 00:18:10,598
The actual place the Lord Jesus came to

358
00:18:10,598 --> 00:18:13,754
was right on the north shore of the Sea of
Galilee,

359
00:18:13,754 --> 00:18:16,292
in the region of a town called Capernaum.

360
00:18:16,292 --> 00:18:23,718
By then the Lord had already done many
signs and wonders, so many had been
helped, and His fame had spread far and
wide.

361
00:18:23,718 --> 00:18:29,722
He went into a certain house, and so many
people came to Him that they crowded in
all around Him,

362
00:18:29,722 --> 00:18:33,930
until there was no room left anywhere, not
even outside at the door.

363
00:18:33,930 --> 00:18:39,810
And there was a certain paralyzed man —
paralyzed, meaning that he simply couldn't
walk at all.

364
00:18:39,810 --> 00:18:45,751
But here's the precious part — he happened
to have four friends, four men who carried
him along.

365
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:50,251
The paralyzed man lay there upon his mat,
completely unable to move himself,

366
00:18:50,251 --> 00:18:53,028
and I find this detail really quite
meaningful.

367
00:18:53,028 --> 00:18:57,046
I wonder if you've ever noticed that
sometimes a person's whole life

368
00:18:57,046 --> 00:19:01,891
is ruled entirely by his circumstances, as
though he can't govern himself at all —

369
00:19:01,891 --> 00:19:06,086
wherever that mat happens to be carried,
that is exactly where he goes.

370
00:19:06,086 --> 00:19:11,699
So the four friends each took hold of a
corner and carried the paralytic right
before the Lord,

371
00:19:11,699 --> 00:19:15,244
all of them hoping that the Lord would be
able to help them.

372
00:19:15,244 --> 00:19:20,326
But there were so very many people there
that they simply couldn't get into the
house,

373
00:19:20,326 --> 00:19:23,871
and so they climbed up onto the roof and
tore the roof open.

374
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:28,480
Then they lowered the paralytic down, mat
and all, right down before the Lord.

375
00:19:28,480 --> 00:19:32,852
Now you might well say — were they really
allowed to do a thing like that?

376
00:19:32,852 --> 00:19:37,756
So let me show you what daily life was
actually like for people back in those
days.

377
00:19:37,756 --> 00:19:41,656
The houses that people lived in looked
something rather like this.

378
00:19:41,656 --> 00:19:45,024
Notice that the roof is only one story up
off the ground,

379
00:19:45,024 --> 00:19:49,101
and that the roof was usually quite flat,
used for drying things out.

380
00:19:49,101 --> 00:19:53,237
And there was a staircase on the outside
leading right up to the roof.

381
00:19:53,237 --> 00:19:57,432
So the four men carried the paralyzed man
all the way up onto the roof.

382
00:19:57,432 --> 00:19:59,914
And what exactly were those roofs made of?

383
00:19:59,914 --> 00:20:00,217
Well,

384
00:20:00,217 --> 00:20:02,158
back then they were very simple:

385
00:20:02,158 --> 00:20:04,342
just a few wooden beams laid across,

386
00:20:04,342 --> 00:20:06,587
covered over with branches and straw,

387
00:20:06,587 --> 00:20:09,013
and then a layer of clay on top of that.

388
00:20:09,013 --> 00:20:10,608
So after every single rain,

389
00:20:10,608 --> 00:20:13,208
they would have to take a heavy stone
roller

390
00:20:13,208 --> 00:20:15,985
and roll it over to flatten the roof out
again,

391
00:20:15,985 --> 00:20:18,349
and then leave it to dry out in the sun.

392
00:20:18,360 --> 00:20:24,249
So from this you can understand how they
were able to tear open the roof and dig
their way through it.

393
00:20:24,249 --> 00:20:27,020
And by the way, let me mention this in
passing —

394
00:20:27,020 --> 00:20:28,174
you know, in English

395
00:20:28,174 --> 00:20:29,791
there's a particular saying:

396
00:20:29,791 --> 00:20:33,370
when it really pours, people say it's
"raining cats and dogs."

397
00:20:33,370 --> 00:20:36,199
Now what does that have to do with cats
and dogs?

398
00:20:36,199 --> 00:20:38,912
Well, it comes from something rather like
this.

399
00:20:38,912 --> 00:20:42,665
Because back then, people's roofs were
usually topped with straw,

400
00:20:42,665 --> 00:20:44,627
all laid across the top like this.

401
00:20:44,627 --> 00:20:47,052
And many animals — the cats and the dogs —

402
00:20:47,052 --> 00:20:49,535
would make their home up inside that
straw.

403
00:20:49,535 --> 00:20:51,497
So whenever it rained really hard,

404
00:20:51,497 --> 00:20:54,846
they would all come washing and sliding
down off the roof.

405
00:20:54,846 --> 00:20:59,464
And that's the very reason heavy rain came
to be called "raining cats and dogs."

406
00:20:59,464 --> 00:21:03,101
So they tore open the roof and lowered the
man down through it.

407
00:21:03,101 --> 00:21:05,122
And what was it that the Lord said?

408
00:21:05,122 --> 00:21:08,932
The Lord saw their faith — now notice that
carefully, their faith.

409
00:21:08,932 --> 00:21:12,858
And that means not only the paralytic, but
the four friends as well.

410
00:21:12,858 --> 00:21:15,052
So why was it that He saw their faith?

411
00:21:15,052 --> 00:21:18,169
Because you can plainly see what it was
they believed.

412
00:21:18,169 --> 00:21:22,441
They believed that if they could only
bring the paralytic before the Lord,

413
00:21:22,441 --> 00:21:24,750
there would surely be real hope for him.

414
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:27,348
They believed the Lord would be able to
help,

415
00:21:27,348 --> 00:21:30,523
and so they even went so far as to tear
open the roof —

416
00:21:30,523 --> 00:21:33,699
at worst, they could repair it for the
owner afterward,

417
00:21:33,699 --> 00:21:36,816
and they didn't fear the risk of being
scolded for it.

418
00:21:36,816 --> 00:21:39,529
Braving the very real chance of a sharp
rebuke,

419
00:21:39,529 --> 00:21:43,859
they still tore open that roof to lower
the paralytic down before the Lord.

420
00:21:43,859 --> 00:21:46,630
And so you can see just how much they
wanted it,

421
00:21:46,630 --> 00:21:49,459
and how firmly they believed the Lord
could help.

422
00:21:49,460 --> 00:21:51,830
Today the Lord can help you too,

423
00:21:51,830 --> 00:21:54,422
no matter what situation you're in.

424
00:21:54,422 --> 00:21:56,274
The Lord saw their faith,

425
00:21:56,274 --> 00:21:58,200
and said to the paralytic,

426
00:21:58,200 --> 00:22:01,088
He said, "Son, your sins are forgiven."

427
00:22:01,088 --> 00:22:03,014
What does "Son" mean here?

428
00:22:03,014 --> 00:22:03,532
"Son" —

429
00:22:03,532 --> 00:22:04,421
a young lad.

430
00:22:04,421 --> 00:22:06,569
I find this quite meaningful.

431
00:22:06,569 --> 00:22:09,531
The Lord didn't merely forgive his sins.

432
00:22:09,531 --> 00:22:13,753
You'll notice there's a warmth, a
tenderness in the Lord.

433
00:22:13,753 --> 00:22:16,864
saying, "Son, your sins are now forgiven."

434
00:22:16,864 --> 00:22:18,715
From this too you can see

435
00:22:18,715 --> 00:22:20,641
that some illnesses today,

436
00:22:20,641 --> 00:22:23,677
and some troubles, are brought on by sin.

437
00:22:23,677 --> 00:22:28,862
Truly — for instance, why do some people
struggle with mental illness?

438
00:22:28,862 --> 00:22:31,899
Because sometimes they harbor resentment,

439
00:22:31,899 --> 00:22:34,565
they're angry, unwilling to forgive,

440
00:22:34,565 --> 00:22:37,453
dwelling on it, brooding day and night,

441
00:22:37,453 --> 00:22:39,305
and it ends up like this.

442
00:22:39,305 --> 00:22:42,786
Some keep turning over how others wronged
them,

443
00:22:42,786 --> 00:22:45,897
some dwell on all kinds of lustful things,

444
00:22:45,897 --> 00:22:48,489
and in the end it affects the body.

445
00:22:48,489 --> 00:22:49,600
So you see, sin

446
00:22:49,600 --> 00:22:50,563
can sometimes

447
00:22:50,563 --> 00:22:51,600
cause a person

448
00:22:51,600 --> 00:22:52,488
to fall ill.

449
00:22:52,488 --> 00:22:56,710
What did the Lord say? He said, "Your sins
are forgiven."

450
00:22:56,710 --> 00:23:01,302
At the time, many people really were
crowding around the Lord,

451
00:23:01,302 --> 00:23:03,376
and there were some scribes,

452
00:23:03,376 --> 00:23:07,079
scribes being those who copied out the
Scriptures.

453
00:23:07,079 --> 00:23:09,893
They knew the Scriptures and knew God,

454
00:23:09,893 --> 00:23:11,004
to some degree.

455
00:23:11,004 --> 00:23:13,745
But a few scribes were sitting there,

456
00:23:13,745 --> 00:23:17,744
which shows they'd come early, or held
some standing —

457
00:23:17,744 --> 00:23:21,744
others couldn't even get in, yet they got
to sit here.

458
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:27,016
In their hearts they were reasoning — not
out loud — saying to themselves,

459
00:23:27,016 --> 00:23:29,431
Why does this man speak like this?

460
00:23:29,431 --> 00:23:31,207
He is speaking blasphemy!

461
00:23:31,207 --> 00:23:32,557
For apart from God,

462
00:23:32,557 --> 00:23:34,048
who can forgive sins?

463
00:23:34,048 --> 00:23:35,327
What is blasphemy?

464
00:23:35,327 --> 00:23:37,671
Blasphemy is presumptuous speech,

465
00:23:37,671 --> 00:23:39,234
speech that oversteps.

466
00:23:39,234 --> 00:23:43,780
If He cannot forgive sins and yet says
"your sins are forgiven,"

467
00:23:43,780 --> 00:23:46,692
that is overstepping — that is blasphemy.

468
00:23:46,692 --> 00:23:51,309
So the passage explains it: apart from
God, who can forgive sins?

469
00:23:51,309 --> 00:23:54,576
Of course, only the One who executes
judgment,

470
00:23:54,576 --> 00:23:57,986
who has the authority to condemn a
person's sin,

471
00:23:57,986 --> 00:24:01,466
also has the authority to forgive a
person's sin.

472
00:24:01,466 --> 00:24:06,509
They were reasoning in their hearts —
perhaps just exchanging glances —

473
00:24:06,509 --> 00:24:08,498
but they said nothing aloud.

474
00:24:08,498 --> 00:24:10,487
But what does the Bible say?

475
00:24:10,487 --> 00:24:15,957
Jesus knew in His spirit that they were
reasoning this way within themselves,

476
00:24:15,957 --> 00:24:17,377
and He said to them,

477
00:24:17,377 --> 00:24:20,716
"Why do you reason these things in your
hearts?

478
00:24:20,716 --> 00:24:25,546
Which is easier — to say to the paralytic,
'Your sins are forgiven,'

479
00:24:25,546 --> 00:24:28,742
or to say, 'Rise, take up your mat and
walk'?

480
00:24:28,742 --> 00:24:31,370
Which of these two is easier to say?"

481
00:24:31,370 --> 00:24:36,982
"But that you may know the Son of Man has
authority on earth to forgive sins" —

482
00:24:36,982 --> 00:24:39,113
then He said to the paralytic,

483
00:24:39,113 --> 00:24:43,303
He said, "I tell you, rise, take up your
mat, and go home."

484
00:24:43,303 --> 00:24:47,068
I think from this passage you can see
several things.

485
00:24:47,068 --> 00:24:49,128
First, who is the Lord Jesus?

486
00:24:49,128 --> 00:24:52,893
He actually knew the thoughts within
people's hearts.

487
00:24:52,900 --> 00:24:56,636
Perhaps they really were just glancing at
one another,

488
00:24:56,636 --> 00:24:58,920
and the Lord saw their reaction —

489
00:24:58,920 --> 00:25:02,172
the Lord's heart may simply be very
perceptive.

490
00:25:02,172 --> 00:25:03,901
But what you see is this:

491
00:25:03,901 --> 00:25:06,669
even the reasoning within their hearts —

492
00:25:06,669 --> 00:25:07,361
the "why —

493
00:25:07,361 --> 00:25:11,374
why is your saying that this young man's
sins are forgiven

494
00:25:11,374 --> 00:25:12,274
blasphemy?" —

495
00:25:12,274 --> 00:25:14,695
the Lord knew this doubt of theirs,

496
00:25:14,695 --> 00:25:17,186
and the Lord put a question to them.

497
00:25:17,186 --> 00:25:18,293
He said to them,

498
00:25:18,293 --> 00:25:23,483
is it easier to forgive sins, or to say,
"Rise, take up your mat and walk"?

499
00:25:23,483 --> 00:25:28,257
Let me ask you all: which of these two do
you think is easier to say?

500
00:25:28,257 --> 00:25:29,572
For people, for me,

501
00:25:29,572 --> 00:25:31,163
perhaps for all of you,

502
00:25:31,163 --> 00:25:34,830
of course "your sins are forgiven" is the
easier one.

503
00:25:34,830 --> 00:25:35,661
Why is that?

504
00:25:35,661 --> 00:25:39,051
After you say it, are the sins actually
forgiven?

505
00:25:39,051 --> 00:25:39,950
Who can tell?

506
00:25:39,950 --> 00:25:42,856
You can't see it; nothing seems to happen.

507
00:25:42,856 --> 00:25:45,140
You just say it, and that's that.

508
00:25:45,140 --> 00:25:47,907
Some people say it and leave it at that.

509
00:25:47,907 --> 00:25:51,921
So "your sins are forgiven" seems the
easier thing to say.

510
00:25:51,921 --> 00:25:55,865
But if you tell him to rise and take up
his mat and walk,

511
00:25:55,865 --> 00:26:00,570
and then the paralytic struggles for
minutes and still can't get up,

512
00:26:00,570 --> 00:26:02,023
well, that's trouble.

513
00:26:02,023 --> 00:26:02,715
Right away

514
00:26:02,715 --> 00:26:05,275
it tests whether your words are true.

515
00:26:05,275 --> 00:26:09,980
So for people, "your sins are forgiven"
might seem the easier thing,

516
00:26:09,980 --> 00:26:13,024
but in the Lord's heart, in the Lord's
eyes,

517
00:26:13,024 --> 00:26:16,760
forgiving a person's sin is actually the
harder thing.

518
00:26:16,760 --> 00:26:17,660
It is harder.

519
00:26:17,660 --> 00:26:20,774
We'll explain a little later why it's
harder.

520
00:26:20,774 --> 00:26:23,610
But the Lord said: so that you may know —

521
00:26:23,610 --> 00:26:26,586
"the Son of Man" refers to the Lord Jesus
—

522
00:26:26,586 --> 00:26:29,907
the Lord has authority on earth to forgive
sins.

523
00:26:29,920 --> 00:26:32,259
So the Lord said to the paralytic,

524
00:26:32,259 --> 00:26:34,598
"Rise, take up your mat and walk."

525
00:26:34,598 --> 00:26:37,418
I think the Lord is truly so considerate.

526
00:26:37,418 --> 00:26:38,932
He told him to get up,

527
00:26:38,932 --> 00:26:41,408
and the paralytic really did get up,

528
00:26:41,408 --> 00:26:43,472
picked up his mat, and walked.

529
00:26:43,472 --> 00:26:48,562
The Lord wasn't fussing over the mat — as
if to say, you dropped this mat,

530
00:26:48,562 --> 00:26:52,690
it's dirty, take it with you, don't leave
your trash behind.

531
00:26:52,690 --> 00:26:58,193
As I said, the mat was like a circumstance
ruling over him; before, he was lame,

532
00:26:58,193 --> 00:27:01,426
couldn't walk — wherever the mat went, he
went.

533
00:27:01,426 --> 00:27:06,586
But today the Lord enabled him to walk;
now he could carry the mat himself.

534
00:27:06,586 --> 00:27:10,919
No longer ruled by his circumstances, he
could now handle them,

535
00:27:10,919 --> 00:27:16,423
he could deal with them. Those who believe
in the Lord today are just like this.

536
00:27:16,423 --> 00:27:20,137
It's not that nothing happens to us in our
experience,

537
00:27:20,137 --> 00:27:23,646
but rather that all kinds of things happen
in life,

538
00:27:23,646 --> 00:27:27,223
and I'm able to handle them, able to deal
with them.

539
00:27:27,223 --> 00:27:29,355
The Lord gives us this ability.

540
00:27:29,355 --> 00:27:32,726
The man got up at once, took his mat, and
walked.

541
00:27:32,726 --> 00:27:34,996
What did the people there record?

542
00:27:34,996 --> 00:27:38,229
They were all amazed — astonished, taken
aback.

543
00:27:38,229 --> 00:27:40,912
Seeing it, they gave glory to God. Why?

544
00:27:40,912 --> 00:27:43,320
Because this was clearly a miracle.

545
00:27:43,320 --> 00:27:45,797
That is, if He had spoken blasphemy,

546
00:27:45,797 --> 00:27:48,273
how could He then perform a miracle?

547
00:27:48,273 --> 00:27:51,506
The Lord's clear performing of a miracle
proves

548
00:27:51,506 --> 00:27:54,189
that He truly had not spoken blasphemy.

549
00:27:54,189 --> 00:27:56,046
He was not blaspheming God.

550
00:27:56,046 --> 00:27:57,285
And if that is so,

551
00:27:57,285 --> 00:28:01,756
then the Lord truly does have authority to
forgive people's sins.

552
00:28:01,756 --> 00:28:03,682
So those people were amazed:

553
00:28:03,682 --> 00:28:06,434
"We have never seen anything like this!"

554
00:28:06,440 --> 00:28:09,461
They had truly never once seen such a
thing before —

555
00:28:09,461 --> 00:28:11,611
and it's not that they had never seen

556
00:28:11,611 --> 00:28:12,599
a lame man before

557
00:28:12,599 --> 00:28:14,749
get healed and be made to walk again.

558
00:28:14,749 --> 00:28:15,330
After all,

559
00:28:15,330 --> 00:28:20,152
the Lord had already performed miracles
and healed a great many people before
this.

560
00:28:20,152 --> 00:28:22,941
At the very least, those four friends
themselves

561
00:28:22,941 --> 00:28:24,568
had this very kind of faith,

562
00:28:24,568 --> 00:28:30,379
believing that bringing the paralytic
right before the Lord would surely bring
him healing and help.

563
00:28:30,379 --> 00:28:34,039
So when they say, "We have never once seen
anything like this,"

564
00:28:34,039 --> 00:28:37,351
it doesn't merely mean a lame man getting
up and walking,

565
00:28:37,351 --> 00:28:39,385
but rather that here on this earth,

566
00:28:39,385 --> 00:28:43,917
God could actually grant to a man the very
authority to forgive people's sins.

567
00:28:43,917 --> 00:28:46,357
And by their very own words they had said,

568
00:28:46,357 --> 00:28:49,669
apart from God alone, who else can
possibly forgive sins?

569
00:28:49,669 --> 00:28:52,981
But the Lord had clearly and plainly
performed a miracle,

570
00:28:52,981 --> 00:28:56,119
and this proved that He truly is able to
forgive sins.

571
00:28:56,119 --> 00:29:00,302
And that means the One standing right
there before their very eyes was —

572
00:29:00,302 --> 00:29:02,859
none other than the Son of God, God
Himself.

573
00:29:02,859 --> 00:29:04,428
Now do you understand this?

574
00:29:04,428 --> 00:29:07,042
The Bible tells us that God is not only
love,

575
00:29:07,042 --> 00:29:09,308
longing so deeply for people to receive

576
00:29:09,308 --> 00:29:10,470
all of His goodness,

577
00:29:10,470 --> 00:29:11,749
and all of His riches,

578
00:29:11,749 --> 00:29:12,911
and all of His love.

579
00:29:12,911 --> 00:29:15,816
The Bible also tells us plainly that God
is light,

580
00:29:15,816 --> 00:29:19,360
and wherever there is light, there can be
no darkness at all.

581
00:29:19,360 --> 00:29:23,021
Now you just said that God is so real, and
that He is so good —

582
00:29:23,021 --> 00:29:27,611
so then why is it that I can't feel Him,
why can't I experience Him for myself?

583
00:29:27,611 --> 00:29:30,690
Well, this picture here explains the whole
situation.

584
00:29:30,690 --> 00:29:33,073
God is still light, and He is still love,

585
00:29:33,073 --> 00:29:36,385
but today so many people are completely
cut off from God,

586
00:29:36,385 --> 00:29:38,883
and what exactly is this wall between
them?

587
00:29:38,883 --> 00:29:42,176
It is nothing other than the sin that they
have committed.

588
00:29:42,176 --> 00:29:45,981
The Bible says that it is our sins that
have separated us from God.

589
00:29:45,981 --> 00:29:47,457
This very thick wall here,

590
00:29:47,457 --> 00:29:48,763
this great wall of sin,

591
00:29:48,763 --> 00:29:50,694
has walled us right off from God —

592
00:29:50,694 --> 00:29:52,681
and it has not merely separated us,

593
00:29:52,681 --> 00:29:54,895
but has cut us off from Him completely,

594
00:29:54,895 --> 00:29:57,167
so that we can no longer see God at all,

595
00:29:57,167 --> 00:29:58,473
can no longer feel Him,

596
00:29:58,473 --> 00:30:00,346
and can no longer experience Him,

597
00:30:00,346 --> 00:30:03,412
and we ourselves are left in great pain
because of it.

598
00:30:03,412 --> 00:30:04,321
And why is that?

599
00:30:04,321 --> 00:30:07,898
Because once we are cut off from the God
of light and holiness,

600
00:30:07,898 --> 00:30:11,759
life is left without any hope, and is
lived out down in the shadows,

601
00:30:11,759 --> 00:30:13,974
still carrying about the burden of sin,

602
00:30:13,974 --> 00:30:16,302
and weighed right down by its heavy load.

603
00:30:16,302 --> 00:30:17,551
You see this man here,

604
00:30:17,551 --> 00:30:19,254
all bound up by a heavy chain.

605
00:30:19,254 --> 00:30:21,696
Now if you were to ask a great many
people,

606
00:30:21,696 --> 00:30:23,399
do you really want to be good?

607
00:30:23,399 --> 00:30:25,727
Do you want to stop cursing and swearing?

608
00:30:25,727 --> 00:30:27,601
Do you want to stop telling lies?

609
00:30:27,601 --> 00:30:29,929
Do you want to stop flying into a temper?

610
00:30:29,929 --> 00:30:31,860
A great many people will tell you,

611
00:30:31,860 --> 00:30:32,995
why, of course I do.

612
00:30:32,995 --> 00:30:35,153
After all, who really wants to be bad?

613
00:30:35,153 --> 00:30:36,800
But here is the real problem,

614
00:30:36,800 --> 00:30:41,967
once a person has sinned, he becomes a
slave to that sin, and he simply cannot
overcome it.

615
00:30:41,967 --> 00:30:45,998
There was once a man who used to curse,
and he tried his very hardest —

616
00:30:45,998 --> 00:30:51,108
he made a New Year's resolution to stop
his cursing; one day was fine, two days
were fine,

617
00:30:51,108 --> 00:30:56,559
but before even a week was out he was
right back at it again, and even worse
than he was before.

618
00:30:56,559 --> 00:30:59,228
So you see, to sin is to become a slave to
sin.

619
00:30:59,228 --> 00:31:03,771
And not only that — there are real
consequences as well: sin brings about
death,

620
00:31:03,771 --> 00:31:06,894
and even after death, there still remains
the judgment.

621
00:31:06,894 --> 00:31:10,982
Now you might well say, but I've never
murdered anyone or set any fires,

622
00:31:10,982 --> 00:31:14,502
I've committed no crime at all, and I have
no criminal record,

623
00:31:14,502 --> 00:31:20,805
I even hold a certificate of good conduct
— that's the very reason I was able to
immigrate here to New Zealand.

624
00:31:20,805 --> 00:31:25,033
Murder, arson, rape, and pillage — all of
those things, of course, are sins.

625
00:31:25,033 --> 00:31:27,871
But what is it that the Bible actually
says sin is?

626
00:31:27,871 --> 00:31:31,765
It says that anything at all which goes
against the conscience is sin.

627
00:31:31,765 --> 00:31:33,435
Now it's a very curious thing.

628
00:31:33,435 --> 00:31:36,828
Today may well be the very first time that
I've ever met you,

629
00:31:36,828 --> 00:31:38,553
and yet deep in your own heart,

630
00:31:38,553 --> 00:31:41,391
you already know that what I'm telling you
is true.

631
00:31:41,391 --> 00:31:43,727
You see, you have a conscience within you.

632
00:31:43,727 --> 00:31:46,454
You already know what is right and what is
wrong,

633
00:31:46,454 --> 00:31:49,903
and these aren't things that you ever
learned out of any book.

634
00:31:49,903 --> 00:31:51,906
You don't need to raise up your hand

635
00:31:51,906 --> 00:31:58,249
and ask, "Teacher, is it wrong to cheat on
the exam?" You don't need to ask at all —
you already know in yourself.

636
00:31:58,249 --> 00:32:00,530
And you won't go and ask your own mother,

637
00:32:00,530 --> 00:32:03,256
"Mother, is it wrong for me to steal your
money?"

638
00:32:03,256 --> 00:32:08,097
People simply have a conscience, and
anything that goes against that conscience
is sin.

639
00:32:08,097 --> 00:32:14,217
Now some will say, well, I'm just a bit
petty about things, or I dwell on a few
lustful thoughts now and then,

640
00:32:14,217 --> 00:32:17,277
but I never once acted on it, and I never
hurt anybody.

641
00:32:17,277 --> 00:32:22,173
But one of the truly terrible things about
sin is that you can never take it back
again.

642
00:32:22,173 --> 00:32:25,400
Take that friend I mentioned earlier, the
one who cursed —

643
00:32:25,400 --> 00:32:28,961
cursing away while chatting with others
came very easily to him,

644
00:32:28,961 --> 00:32:31,909
but then on one occasion he got himself
into a fight,

645
00:32:31,909 --> 00:32:36,527
and the whole reason for that fight was
that the other man had cursed at him
first.

646
00:32:36,527 --> 00:32:42,926
So you see, one of the truly terrifying
things about the sinful mindset is just
this: you simply cannot reverse it.

647
00:32:42,926 --> 00:32:45,930
For instance, take a man who dwells on
lustful things.

648
00:32:45,930 --> 00:32:47,766
Take some husbands, for example —

649
00:32:47,766 --> 00:32:51,049
as the old saying goes, "a man who isn't a
bit of a playboy

650
00:32:51,049 --> 00:32:51,716
in his youth

651
00:32:51,716 --> 00:32:57,892
has wasted his youth," and so he takes one
mistress after another. But if his wife
were to turn and say to him,

652
00:32:57,892 --> 00:33:03,567
well, how would you like it if I went and
had myself a lover, and then a second one,
and even a third?

653
00:33:03,567 --> 00:33:10,122
You'd find he would flare right up in
anger. So you see, the real terror of sin
is that he cannot turn it around again,

654
00:33:10,122 --> 00:33:13,757
along with that whole mindset — that
deeply self-centered mindset.

655
00:33:13,757 --> 00:33:16,896
So that is why, in English, sin is
actually called "sin."

656
00:33:16,896 --> 00:33:24,057
The S is for "selfish," the I right there
in the very center — the self placed at
the center — and the N, for nothing else
at all.

657
00:33:24,057 --> 00:33:26,646
And God is light, and He utterly hates all
sin.

658
00:33:26,646 --> 00:33:29,399
Now we were just speaking a moment ago
about sin —

659
00:33:29,399 --> 00:33:32,209
and besides separating a person right off
from God,

660
00:33:32,209 --> 00:33:34,136
and leaving him thoroughly unhappy,

661
00:33:34,136 --> 00:33:36,395
it truly does leave a person's whole life

662
00:33:36,395 --> 00:33:37,716
completely without hope.

663
00:33:37,716 --> 00:33:40,801
with no way out at all. Now I recently saw
a news story.

664
00:33:40,801 --> 00:33:43,114
And what was it that this story was about?

665
00:33:43,114 --> 00:33:45,813
Over in Switzerland they had invented a
so-called

666
00:33:45,813 --> 00:33:47,521
machine designed to help people

667
00:33:47,521 --> 00:33:49,889
end their own lives — a euthanasia
machine.

668
00:33:49,889 --> 00:33:53,029
Now you would find a thing like that very
strange indeed.

669
00:33:53,029 --> 00:33:58,592
Why would people ever take their own lives
— apart, of course, from those with some
terminal illness?

670
00:33:58,592 --> 00:34:00,134
Some people, perhaps, simply

671
00:34:00,134 --> 00:34:03,494
feel that there is nothing left for them
to live for anymore.

672
00:34:03,494 --> 00:34:05,421
You lie yourself down inside of it,

673
00:34:05,421 --> 00:34:09,112
and very soon nitrogen gas is released,
and you lose consciousness,

674
00:34:09,112 --> 00:34:10,709
and then after that, you die.

675
00:34:10,709 --> 00:34:13,463
You might well find the whole thing very
strange —

676
00:34:13,463 --> 00:34:16,382
why, of all the things in the world to go
and invent,

677
00:34:16,382 --> 00:34:19,577
would anyone ever invent a machine for
committing suicide?

678
00:34:19,577 --> 00:34:21,395
From this too you can clearly see

679
00:34:21,395 --> 00:34:23,928
the deep hopelessness that people feel
inside,

680
00:34:23,928 --> 00:34:26,021
once they have been cut off from God —

681
00:34:26,021 --> 00:34:28,885
that terrible darkness with no way out of
it at all.

682
00:34:28,885 --> 00:34:31,529
Earlier on, back while we were leading the
hymn,

683
00:34:31,529 --> 00:34:33,622
I had mentioned this particular verse.

684
00:34:33,622 --> 00:34:35,449
It says: it is appointed

685
00:34:35,449 --> 00:34:37,352
for everyone to die once,

686
00:34:37,352 --> 00:34:41,386
and after death, the judgment. God is
perfectly just.

687
00:34:41,386 --> 00:34:45,039
So the poor will die, but the rich will
die too.

688
00:34:45,039 --> 00:34:47,246
Those with millions will die.

689
00:34:47,246 --> 00:34:50,062
The powerless and oppressed will die,

690
00:34:50,062 --> 00:34:54,477
but the oppressors, the dictators, will
die just the same.

691
00:34:54,477 --> 00:34:58,358
Everyone dies once, but death is not the
end of it.

692
00:34:58,358 --> 00:35:02,697
Each will be judged according to what he
did in his life.

693
00:35:02,697 --> 00:35:04,676
The wages of sin is death,

694
00:35:04,676 --> 00:35:07,340
and all who sin are cast into hell.

695
00:35:07,340 --> 00:35:08,025
Hell is a

696
00:35:08,025 --> 00:35:09,014
lake of fire,

697
00:35:09,014 --> 00:35:11,906
a lake of fire that is never quenched.

698
00:35:11,906 --> 00:35:14,190
There was a recent news story:

699
00:35:14,190 --> 00:35:14,723
someone

700
00:35:14,723 --> 00:35:17,691
took three hundred thousand photographs

701
00:35:17,691 --> 00:35:21,496
and assembled them into a single image —
this one.

702
00:35:21,496 --> 00:35:26,063
It's been called the clearest picture of
the sun ever taken.

703
00:35:26,063 --> 00:35:29,564
Three hundred thousand photos pieced
together.

704
00:35:29,564 --> 00:35:31,543
You see this ball of fire,

705
00:35:31,543 --> 00:35:33,827
burning for billions of years.

706
00:35:33,827 --> 00:35:35,425
If God can make a sun

707
00:35:35,425 --> 00:35:37,175
that burns for so long,

708
00:35:37,175 --> 00:35:40,753
then you can be sure God will, for all who
sin,

709
00:35:40,753 --> 00:35:42,047
prepare a place —

710
00:35:42,047 --> 00:35:42,427
hell,

711
00:35:42,427 --> 00:35:43,569
a lake of fire.

712
00:35:43,569 --> 00:35:45,243
In fact, in the Bible,

713
00:35:45,243 --> 00:35:49,353
the One who spoke most about hell is the
Lord Himself.

714
00:35:49,353 --> 00:35:52,322
He said, if your eye causes you to sin,

715
00:35:52,322 --> 00:35:53,311
pluck it out;

716
00:35:53,311 --> 00:35:56,584
it is better to enter paradise with one
eye

717
00:35:56,584 --> 00:35:59,857
than with both eyes to be thrown into
hell.

718
00:35:59,857 --> 00:36:02,257
If your hand causes you to sin,

719
00:36:02,257 --> 00:36:03,108
cut it off;

720
00:36:03,108 --> 00:36:08,914
better to enter paradise without a hand
than with both hands to go to hell.

721
00:36:08,920 --> 00:36:14,838
But He doesn't mean you should actually
pluck out your eye or cut off your hand —
no.

722
00:36:14,838 --> 00:36:18,110
He means: whatever the cost, do not go to
hell.

723
00:36:18,110 --> 00:36:19,920
The Lord loves you dearly,

724
00:36:19,920 --> 00:36:21,034
He loves people,

725
00:36:21,034 --> 00:36:22,217
and He is saying,

726
00:36:22,217 --> 00:36:24,027
don't come to such an end,

727
00:36:24,027 --> 00:36:25,211
don't go to hell.

728
00:36:25,211 --> 00:36:29,388
So God sent His beloved Son, the Lord
Jesus, into the world,

729
00:36:29,388 --> 00:36:30,919
and most importantly —

730
00:36:30,919 --> 00:36:33,565
yes, He healed many people's diseases,

731
00:36:33,565 --> 00:36:35,584
comforted many broken hearts,

732
00:36:35,584 --> 00:36:36,976
changed many lives —

733
00:36:36,976 --> 00:36:39,413
but the most important thing of all

734
00:36:39,413 --> 00:36:40,945
is that, for our sins,

735
00:36:40,945 --> 00:36:42,546
He bore the punishment.

736
00:36:42,546 --> 00:36:43,381
God is just.

737
00:36:43,381 --> 00:36:45,957
He will by no means clear the guilty.

738
00:36:45,957 --> 00:36:47,906
If a judge found you guilty,

739
00:36:47,906 --> 00:36:51,387
and said, "I love you, so I declare you
innocent,"

740
00:36:51,387 --> 00:36:54,172
then something is wrong with that judge.

741
00:36:54,172 --> 00:36:58,419
That judge himself is at fault, that judge
himself is unjust,

742
00:36:58,419 --> 00:37:01,204
because he's covering for you, isn't he?

743
00:37:01,204 --> 00:37:03,222
So when God would forgive us,

744
00:37:03,222 --> 00:37:05,938
He had to do it in a way that was just.

745
00:37:05,938 --> 00:37:08,931
That's why, with the paralytic we spoke
of,

746
00:37:08,931 --> 00:37:12,064
when the Lord said, "Your sins are
forgiven,"

747
00:37:12,064 --> 00:37:14,849
it was in fact a very hard thing to say.

748
00:37:14,849 --> 00:37:19,304
Yet from the very start the Lord spoke to
him the hardest words,

749
00:37:19,304 --> 00:37:21,393
declaring that He was willing.

750
00:37:21,393 --> 00:37:24,108
When He said He forgave that man's sin,

751
00:37:24,108 --> 00:37:26,197
perhaps He already had in mind

752
00:37:26,197 --> 00:37:27,798
that one day, for him —

753
00:37:27,798 --> 00:37:31,209
for the sins of mankind — He would pay the
price.

754
00:37:31,209 --> 00:37:33,228
But the Lord Jesus' greatest,

755
00:37:33,228 --> 00:37:35,177
most important act was this:

756
00:37:35,177 --> 00:37:37,684
to bear the punishment for our sins,

757
00:37:37,684 --> 00:37:39,215
hanging upon the tree.

758
00:37:39,220 --> 00:37:41,009
So this is why the Bible says

759
00:37:41,009 --> 00:37:41,995
that He loved me

760
00:37:41,995 --> 00:37:44,771
and that He gave His very own self up for
me.

761
00:37:44,771 --> 00:37:47,423
Now in the Lord Jesus' final days on
earth,

762
00:37:47,423 --> 00:37:50,568
He had done so many miracles and so very
much good,

763
00:37:50,568 --> 00:37:54,947
and yet, out of sheer hatred and jealousy,
the people came to hate Him,

764
00:37:54,947 --> 00:37:58,771
hating Him entirely without cause, and
seeking to destroy Him.

765
00:37:58,771 --> 00:38:02,842
They used a great many false witnesses in
order to frame the Lord,

766
00:38:02,842 --> 00:38:05,309
speaking all manner of lies against Him,

767
00:38:05,309 --> 00:38:09,133
claiming that He had said things which He
had never once said,

768
00:38:09,133 --> 00:38:11,477
all in order to force His crucifixion.

769
00:38:11,477 --> 00:38:14,992
Now crucifixion was a most cruel and
terrible punishment.

770
00:38:14,992 --> 00:38:22,270
Before He was ever nailed to the cross,
they wove together a crown of thorns and
pressed it down onto the Lord's head,

771
00:38:22,270 --> 00:38:27,513
and they draped a purple robe over Him,
all the while mocking Him and jeering at
Him.

772
00:38:27,513 --> 00:38:32,508
As we said earlier, "Bethlehem Ephrathah —
out of you shall come forth a ruler" —

773
00:38:32,508 --> 00:38:39,231
So you're the king, are you? You're the
one who's going to rule? Congratulations
to you, they sneered at Him.

774
00:38:39,231 --> 00:38:44,720
So they crowned Him with those thorns, and
robed Him in that purple, and they mocked
Him,

775
00:38:44,720 --> 00:38:50,641
and they struck Him with their hands, and
spat right into His face — oh, a terrible
humiliation.

776
00:38:50,641 --> 00:38:53,478
And what is it that the Bible says about
this?

777
00:38:53,478 --> 00:39:00,078
Yet the Lord set His face like a flint,
for He was fully determined to go through
all of this for our sake.

778
00:39:00,078 --> 00:39:05,628
Three nails fixed Him fast to the cross;
and even before that, they had scourged
the Lord.

779
00:39:05,628 --> 00:39:11,673
The whip they used was a cat-o'-nine-tails
— a single whip splitting out into nine
separate tails.

780
00:39:11,680 --> 00:39:14,253
An ordinary whip lands with a crack,

781
00:39:14,253 --> 00:39:17,327
but this one had bits of metal on the
ends,

782
00:39:17,327 --> 00:39:21,545
sinking into the flesh and tearing it out
in a bloody mess.

783
00:39:21,545 --> 00:39:23,689
The Bible says the Lord's back

784
00:39:23,689 --> 00:39:25,977
was like a field plowed by oxen,

785
00:39:25,977 --> 00:39:27,835
its furrows deep and long.

786
00:39:27,835 --> 00:39:29,694
There are records of this:

787
00:39:29,694 --> 00:39:32,696
some people died from the scourging alone,

788
00:39:32,696 --> 00:39:35,913
because even their inner organs were
exposed.

789
00:39:35,913 --> 00:39:38,415
There's not much flesh on the back.

790
00:39:38,415 --> 00:39:40,416
They beat the Lord terribly.

791
00:39:40,416 --> 00:39:43,847
Why does it dwell on how severely He was
beaten?

792
00:39:43,847 --> 00:39:46,778
Because the governor at the time, Pilate,

793
00:39:46,778 --> 00:39:50,138
wanted to use this to win the crowd's
sympathy.

794
00:39:50,138 --> 00:39:51,282
He said to them,

795
00:39:51,282 --> 00:39:53,426
I find no fault in this Jesus,

796
00:39:53,426 --> 00:39:55,142
yet he had Him scourged,

797
00:39:55,142 --> 00:39:57,930
tormented until He hardly looked human,

798
00:39:57,930 --> 00:40:00,146
then brought the Lord Jesus out

799
00:40:00,146 --> 00:40:01,361
and said to them,

800
00:40:01,361 --> 00:40:02,433
Behold the man!

801
00:40:02,433 --> 00:40:05,078
He's already been beaten so severely.

802
00:40:05,078 --> 00:40:08,009
His aim was to stir the crowd's sympathy.

803
00:40:08,009 --> 00:40:10,725
I find not the slightest guilt in Him,

804
00:40:10,725 --> 00:40:14,228
I know it's out of envy that you handed
Him over,

805
00:40:14,228 --> 00:40:18,803
and I've already had Him beaten like this
— it should be enough.

806
00:40:18,803 --> 00:40:22,234
But those people were set on rejecting the
Lord.

807
00:40:22,234 --> 00:40:23,949
They would not have Him.

808
00:40:23,949 --> 00:40:26,094
They demanded He be crucified.

809
00:40:26,094 --> 00:40:30,383
So with three nails, a man of over a
hundred pounds was hung

810
00:40:30,383 --> 00:40:31,384
upon the wood.

811
00:40:31,384 --> 00:40:32,027
In fact —

812
00:40:32,027 --> 00:40:33,028
just imagine —

813
00:40:33,028 --> 00:40:34,386
He is the true God,

814
00:40:34,386 --> 00:40:40,390
the One who made heaven and earth; yet the
Maker of heaven and earth, in this world,

815
00:40:40,390 --> 00:40:43,178
could not find a single place to stand,

816
00:40:43,178 --> 00:40:46,609
hung between heaven and earth, reaching
neither.

817
00:40:50,360 --> 00:40:52,369
Rejected to such a degree.

818
00:40:52,369 --> 00:40:57,855
But there's meaning in it too — hanging
there between heaven and earth,

819
00:40:57,855 --> 00:40:59,091
so that today we

820
00:40:59,091 --> 00:41:01,873
might have a living way back to God.

821
00:41:01,873 --> 00:41:04,114
He became a ladder to heaven.

822
00:41:04,114 --> 00:41:08,054
Three nails held up a man of over a
hundred pounds.

823
00:41:08,054 --> 00:41:12,304
Naturally it was agony, the blood flowing
without stop.

824
00:41:12,304 --> 00:41:16,477
And when you're hung up like that, you
cannot breathe.

825
00:41:16,477 --> 00:41:18,795
Your weight pulls you forward,

826
00:41:18,795 --> 00:41:20,804
and you can't draw breath.

827
00:41:20,804 --> 00:41:25,749
So each time you breathe, you have to push
yourself up and back,

828
00:41:25,749 --> 00:41:28,453
but your back has been flayed open.

829
00:41:28,453 --> 00:41:30,385
Each time you press back,

830
00:41:30,385 --> 00:41:31,389
your raw back

831
00:41:31,389 --> 00:41:34,171
scrapes against the splintered wood,

832
00:41:34,171 --> 00:41:36,644
so every single breath is agony.

833
00:41:36,644 --> 00:41:38,189
With every movement,

834
00:41:38,189 --> 00:41:40,816
the wounds where the nails pierced

835
00:41:40,816 --> 00:41:42,516
tear wider and longer,

836
00:41:42,516 --> 00:41:43,829
wider and longer.

837
00:41:43,829 --> 00:41:50,784
He hung on the cross for six hours, from
nine in the morning until three in the
afternoon.

838
00:41:50,784 --> 00:41:53,333
And at noon, the sky turned dark.

839
00:41:53,333 --> 00:41:57,738
We spoke of that ball of fire, the sun,
burning so long —

840
00:41:57,738 --> 00:42:02,451
yet at midday, from twelve noon until
three in the afternoon,

841
00:42:02,451 --> 00:42:06,469
the Bible says darkness came over all the
land. Why?

842
00:42:06,469 --> 00:42:07,980
I find it striking:

843
00:42:07,980 --> 00:42:11,400
this was the darkest hour in the universe
—

844
00:42:11,400 --> 00:42:14,105
the One who least deserved to die,

845
00:42:14,105 --> 00:42:14,582
dying;

846
00:42:14,582 --> 00:42:18,214
the One without sin, hung upon the tree
for us.

847
00:42:18,214 --> 00:42:23,313
This was no solar eclipse, for an eclipse
never lasts three hours,

848
00:42:23,313 --> 00:42:28,413
and besides, if you know that day was the
fourteenth of the month,

849
00:42:28,413 --> 00:42:33,745
the moon was not between the sun and the
earth; the moon was far off,

850
00:42:33,745 --> 00:42:37,531
with the earth in between — so it was no
eclipse.

851
00:42:39,940 --> 00:42:43,711
Now if you were to ask me why it was that
the whole land went dark,

852
00:42:43,711 --> 00:42:46,750
whether the sun itself withheld its light
for a time —

853
00:42:46,750 --> 00:42:49,338
well, I honestly don't know the reason for
it.

854
00:42:49,338 --> 00:42:55,416
But it does seem to be saying something to
us: that God wanted all people to take
careful note of one thing.

855
00:42:55,416 --> 00:42:58,905
It's just like on a stage, when all the
lights suddenly go out

856
00:42:58,905 --> 00:43:03,351
and a single spotlight comes to fall right
on the center, right upon the Lord —

857
00:43:03,351 --> 00:43:06,447
everyone there simply must pay close
attention to this.

858
00:43:06,447 --> 00:43:08,529
As all of heaven and earth went dark,

859
00:43:08,529 --> 00:43:12,074
every last person ought to take careful
note of this one thing:

860
00:43:12,074 --> 00:43:13,650
that the Son of God Himself,

861
00:43:13,650 --> 00:43:15,451
hung there upon the tree for us,

862
00:43:15,451 --> 00:43:17,308
and became a curse on our behalf,

863
00:43:17,308 --> 00:43:19,334
bearing the full weight of our sins.

864
00:43:19,334 --> 00:43:20,797
And so at this very point,

865
00:43:20,797 --> 00:43:24,005
I would very much love to share a hymn
together with you.

866
00:43:24,005 --> 00:43:25,693
This particular hymn is called

867
00:43:25,693 --> 00:43:26,031
"Come,

868
00:43:26,031 --> 00:43:26,875
Come and Feel."

869
00:43:26,875 --> 00:43:30,589
And I do hope that you will take in the
Lord's great love for you,

870
00:43:30,589 --> 00:43:34,641
and His whole heart toward you — just
where His love for you truly lies.

871
00:43:34,641 --> 00:43:39,200
He was so willing to pass through every
last suffering and every hardship for us.

872
00:44:01,200 --> 00:44:08,140
God's love is displayed upon the cross;

873
00:44:08,140 --> 00:44:15,240
for me the Lord endured torment and scorn,

874
00:44:15,240 --> 00:44:21,900
shamed by men,

875
00:44:21,900 --> 00:44:26,800
heaped with slander.

876
00:44:26,800 --> 00:44:31,300
The Father's beloved Son tasted

877
00:44:31,300 --> 00:44:35,800
every mockery and torment,

878
00:44:35,800 --> 00:44:40,244
crowned with thorns,

879
00:44:40,244 --> 00:44:45,800
and cruelly scourged,

880
00:44:45,800 --> 00:44:50,164
His body covered

881
00:44:50,164 --> 00:44:54,800
over with wounds.

882
00:44:54,800 --> 00:44:59,244
Hands and feet nailed fast,

883
00:44:59,244 --> 00:45:04,800
hung high upon the wood,

884
00:45:04,800 --> 00:45:08,800
in utter agony —

885
00:45:08,800 --> 00:45:13,800
who can feel it?

886
00:45:24,800 --> 00:45:34,025
The pain

887
00:45:34,025 --> 00:45:54,780
that never ceases.

888
00:45:54,780 --> 00:46:00,040
His face gaunt and wasted,

889
00:46:00,040 --> 00:46:07,040
hung on the cross, His bones now all laid
bare,

890
00:46:07,040 --> 00:46:14,400
blood streaming down His face,

891
00:46:14,400 --> 00:46:19,040
dripping to the ground,

892
00:46:19,040 --> 00:46:21,400
sorely wounded,

893
00:46:21,400 --> 00:46:28,200
yet struck even by the Father.

894
00:46:28,200 --> 00:46:32,467
Who could write a poem

895
00:46:32,467 --> 00:46:37,800
to capture such love?

896
00:46:37,800 --> 00:46:41,978
His love,

897
00:46:41,978 --> 00:46:47,200
engraved within my heart.

898
00:46:47,200 --> 00:46:51,422
How fresh His mercy,

899
00:46:51,422 --> 00:46:56,700
deep and wide —

900
00:46:56,700 --> 00:47:00,700
the grace of the cross,

901
00:47:00,700 --> 00:47:05,700
who can ever fathom it?

902
00:47:05,700 --> 00:47:09,700
My Lord even

903
00:47:09,700 --> 00:47:14,700
cried out, "It is finished."

904
00:47:14,700 --> 00:47:18,300
I will ponder it

905
00:47:18,300 --> 00:47:23,700
ten thousand times over.

906
00:47:23,700 --> 00:47:28,144
Jesus, my Lord,

907
00:47:28,144 --> 00:47:33,700
Your love runs deep and will never die.

908
00:47:33,700 --> 00:47:37,700
This grace

909
00:47:37,700 --> 00:47:42,700
forever moves us.

910
00:47:42,700 --> 00:47:48,140
This deep grace —

911
00:47:48,140 --> 00:47:49,740
come,

912
00:47:49,740 --> 00:47:53,580
and feel it.

913
00:48:15,000 --> 00:48:21,923
He loved me and gave Himself for me.

914
00:48:21,923 --> 00:48:25,000
(Galatians 2:20)

915
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:38,000
As the hymn just mentioned, there on the
cross, at the very end, the Lord cried out
aloud: "It is finished."

916
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:37,739
As the hymn just mentioned, there on the
cross, at the very end, the Lord cried out
aloud: "It is finished."

917
00:48:37,739 --> 00:48:41,250
He had carried this one single purpose all
along:

918
00:48:41,250 --> 00:48:43,257
to deal fully with our sins,

919
00:48:43,257 --> 00:48:45,335
and to bear our sins Himself,

920
00:48:45,335 --> 00:48:45,836
so that

921
00:48:45,836 --> 00:48:48,631
today our sins might truly be forgiven.

922
00:48:48,631 --> 00:48:50,852
He cried out, "It is finished."

923
00:48:50,852 --> 00:48:54,220
He had fully accomplished this great
salvation.

924
00:48:54,220 --> 00:48:56,298
And so it turns out that God,

925
00:48:56,298 --> 00:48:58,090
in just exactly this way,

926
00:48:58,090 --> 00:49:00,024
had set out to save us all.

927
00:49:00,024 --> 00:49:03,464
The Bible says we, like sheep, have gone
astray,

928
00:49:03,464 --> 00:49:06,187
each one of us turning to his own way,

929
00:49:06,187 --> 00:49:10,844
and God the Father laid on the Lord Jesus
the iniquity of us all.

930
00:49:10,844 --> 00:49:15,860
God used this very method of substitution
in order to save you and me,

931
00:49:15,860 --> 00:49:18,870
crushing His own beloved Son in our place,

932
00:49:18,870 --> 00:49:21,450
and making Him our sin-bearing Lamb.

933
00:49:21,450 --> 00:49:24,603
So the Lord Jesus is indeed the Lamb of
God,

934
00:49:24,603 --> 00:49:27,612
the holy One, utterly without any blemish,

935
00:49:27,612 --> 00:49:31,052
and yet He hung there on the cross for our
sake.

936
00:49:31,052 --> 00:49:31,708
You know,

937
00:49:31,708 --> 00:49:36,663
the Chinese character for "righteousness,"
if you go and look it up,

938
00:49:36,663 --> 00:49:39,651
actually falls under the "sheep" radical.

939
00:49:39,651 --> 00:49:45,240
A lamb standing there in my place — that
is the very picture of righteousness.

940
00:49:45,240 --> 00:49:52,262
So that today we are not only set free
from sin, but are actually counted as
righteous before God.

941
00:49:52,262 --> 00:49:58,210
The Lord died there in our place, and in
doing so He brought us this precious gift,

942
00:49:58,210 --> 00:50:03,871
changing our very lives, and teaching us
what is truly lovely and what is good.

943
00:50:03,880 --> 00:50:07,298
How precious it is — that the Lord did all
of this for us;

944
00:50:07,298 --> 00:50:09,832
and then, on the third day after His
death,

945
00:50:09,832 --> 00:50:11,482
He rose again from the dead.

946
00:50:11,482 --> 00:50:13,663
God raised the Lord up from the dead.

947
00:50:13,663 --> 00:50:16,374
The Lord Jesus rose again from among the
dead,

948
00:50:16,374 --> 00:50:18,849
and this one thing declares to us plainly:

949
00:50:18,849 --> 00:50:21,914
that this salvation has now been fully
accomplished.

950
00:50:21,914 --> 00:50:24,212
For if the Lord Himself had had any sin

951
00:50:24,212 --> 00:50:25,980
and had died on account of it,

952
00:50:25,980 --> 00:50:28,691
then He could never possibly have risen
again.

953
00:50:28,691 --> 00:50:31,107
But the Lord's resurrection from the dead

954
00:50:31,107 --> 00:50:33,642
declares to us that He truly bore our
sins,

955
00:50:33,642 --> 00:50:37,119
and that God Himself accepted this whole
work of salvation.

956
00:50:37,119 --> 00:50:39,122
God raised the Lord up from death,

957
00:50:39,122 --> 00:50:41,480
and exalted Him with His own right hand,

958
00:50:41,480 --> 00:50:44,780
and gave to Him the name that is above
every other name.

959
00:50:44,780 --> 00:50:46,548
And today this same risen Lord

960
00:50:46,548 --> 00:50:49,318
is able to help us walk the whole road of
life,

961
00:50:49,318 --> 00:50:51,734
and He is able to be right there with us,

962
00:50:51,734 --> 00:50:54,268
so that my life is no longer lonely at
all,

963
00:50:54,268 --> 00:50:57,392
and no longer like duckweed drifting
aimlessly about.

964
00:50:57,392 --> 00:50:59,808
He hears every single one of our prayers,

965
00:50:59,808 --> 00:51:03,934
and He is able to teach us, to guide us,
and to change our very lives,

966
00:51:03,934 --> 00:51:08,766
and to bring us all the way home — home to
heaven, back before the Father Himself.

967
00:51:08,766 --> 00:51:14,129
So very many people, coming to know this
salvation, have received the Lord as their
Savior,

968
00:51:14,129 --> 00:51:18,196
and their lives have been changed, and
their sins have been forgiven.

969
00:51:18,196 --> 00:51:20,671
So how is it that you believe in the Lord?

970
00:51:20,671 --> 00:51:25,798
Well, there's no paperwork at all to file;
you need only to pray to the Lord
sincerely.

971
00:51:25,798 --> 00:51:29,040
Lord, today I am willing to repent, and to
sin no more.

972
00:51:29,040 --> 00:51:31,692
Please forgive all the sins of my whole
life,

973
00:51:31,692 --> 00:51:34,579
and I am willing to receive You as my own
Savior.

974
00:51:34,580 --> 00:51:36,445
It really is as simple as that.

975
00:51:36,445 --> 00:51:39,574
The Lord is so very glad indeed to hear
your prayer,

976
00:51:39,574 --> 00:51:40,837
and glad to save you,

977
00:51:40,837 --> 00:51:43,003
and glad to be your very own Savior,

978
00:51:43,003 --> 00:51:46,252
and glad to walk the road of life right
alongside you,

979
00:51:46,252 --> 00:51:49,983
and glad to change both your life now and
your whole eternity,

980
00:51:49,983 --> 00:51:52,450
so that all those who believe in the Lord

981
00:51:52,450 --> 00:51:54,856
have their lives truly changed for good,

982
00:51:54,856 --> 00:51:56,541
and all their sins forgiven,

983
00:51:56,541 --> 00:51:58,466
and are fully reconciled to God,

984
00:51:58,466 --> 00:52:00,632
and become the very children of God,

985
00:52:00,632 --> 00:52:02,919
with an abundant and overflowing life.

986
00:52:02,919 --> 00:52:05,566
He said He came that people might have
life,

987
00:52:05,566 --> 00:52:07,311
and have it more abundantly —

988
00:52:07,311 --> 00:52:08,996
to enjoy real and true love,

989
00:52:08,996 --> 00:52:10,379
and real peace and joy,

990
00:52:10,379 --> 00:52:12,846
and a living hope well worth boasting in:

991
00:52:12,846 --> 00:52:16,998
namely, that we have a bright and warm
home waiting for us in heaven.

992
00:52:16,998 --> 00:52:20,427
So do you long to receive all of this
grace for yourself?

993
00:52:20,427 --> 00:52:23,616
This is the very thing that God has
prepared for you,

994
00:52:23,616 --> 00:52:26,264
and what God so dearly wants to give to
you.

995
00:52:26,264 --> 00:52:29,874
Now why exactly is this called the
"gospel" — the good news?

996
00:52:29,874 --> 00:52:33,965
Well, it's because He is so willing to
deal fully with all our sins,

997
00:52:33,965 --> 00:52:38,899
and because He wants us to receive the
very greatest and fullest happiness of
all.

998
00:52:38,899 --> 00:52:42,268
So at this point I'd like to give you all
just a moment,

999
00:52:42,268 --> 00:52:44,193
to be quite still, and to think.

1000
00:52:44,193 --> 00:52:47,623
If there are any here among us who have
not yet believed,

1001
00:52:47,623 --> 00:52:51,053
who have not yet received the Lord Jesus
as their Savior,

1002
00:52:51,053 --> 00:52:55,625
I do hope that in this very moment you
will go ahead and make this decision,

1003
00:52:55,625 --> 00:52:57,972
to receive the Lord as your own Savior.

1004
00:52:57,972 --> 00:53:01,943
You can experience for yourself the Lord
changing your whole life,

1005
00:53:01,943 --> 00:53:05,192
so that you are no longer down in the
darkness at all,

1006
00:53:05,192 --> 00:53:07,358
but can enter right into the light —

1007
00:53:07,358 --> 00:53:09,825
and into a truly marvelous light at that.

1008
00:53:09,825 --> 00:53:13,279
Believing in the Lord is a good thing
indeed.

1009
00:53:13,279 --> 00:53:15,890
So please don't hesitate about it.

1010
00:53:15,890 --> 00:53:19,728
The people all around you long for you to
believe,

1011
00:53:19,728 --> 00:53:23,260
because as you change, and as you grow
better,

1012
00:53:23,260 --> 00:53:26,331
that is the very thing they long to see.

1013
00:53:26,331 --> 00:53:28,634
And once you yourself believe,

1014
00:53:28,634 --> 00:53:35,006
they too can come to know the Lord through
your own changed life in the days ahead.

1015
00:53:35,006 --> 00:53:42,914
So I'd like now to invite everyone who is
willing to believe today to pray together
with me, like this.

1016
00:53:42,914 --> 00:53:45,908
You may pray quietly in your own heart,

1017
00:53:45,908 --> 00:53:49,593
or you may pray along with me, phrase by
phrase.

1018
00:53:49,593 --> 00:53:51,129
So let us now begin.

1019
00:53:51,129 --> 00:53:51,973
Lord Jesus,

1020
00:53:51,973 --> 00:53:53,739
I am willing to repent,

1021
00:53:53,739 --> 00:53:55,198
and to sin no more.

1022
00:53:55,198 --> 00:53:57,885
I ask You to forgive my whole life,

1023
00:53:57,885 --> 00:53:59,344
and all of my sins.

1024
00:53:59,344 --> 00:54:01,416
I am willing to receive You

1025
00:54:01,416 --> 00:54:03,413
as my own personal Savior.

1026
00:54:03,413 --> 00:54:05,102
This I sincerely pray.

1027
00:54:05,102 --> 00:54:12,472
And congratulations to every one of you
who believed today and received the Lord
as your Savior.

1028
00:54:12,472 --> 00:54:17,462
This year's Christmas will truly be an
unforgettable one for you,

1029
00:54:17,462 --> 00:54:23,604
for you can now receive and enjoy all the
things that God has prepared for you —

1030
00:54:23,604 --> 00:54:26,368
every blessing, and every happiness.

